desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Visualforce Page API Version"
	title_zh: "检测到 Visualforce API 版本低于 55",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-config-visualforce-page-api-version"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `visualforce-page-api-version` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/generic/visualforce/security/ncino/xml/VisualForceAPIVersion.yaml).
Original message: Visualforce Pages must use API version 55 or higher for required use of the cspHeader attribute set to true.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting (XSS)')
References:
- https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_pages.htm
Note: context-aware regex — version hits are kept only inside `apiVersion` elements.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Upgrade the Visualforce page API version to 55.0 or newer and explicitly set the required cspHeader attributes.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.page-meta.xml": <<<POS
<apiVersion>54.0</apiVersion>
POS
	"safefile://neg.page-meta.xml": <<<NEG
<apiVersion>55.0</apiVersion>
NEG
)

${*.page-meta.xml}.pattern_regex(/<apiVersion[\s\S]*?<\/apiVersion>/) as $ctx
${*.page-meta.xml}.pattern_regex(/>[0-9][0-9]*\.[0-9]</) as $version
${*.page-meta.xml}.pattern_regex(/>[1-4][0-9]\.[0-9]</) as $below50
${*.page-meta.xml}.pattern_regex(/>5[0-4]\.[0-9]</) as $low2
$version inside $ctx as $a
$below50 inside $a as $b
$low2 inside $a as $c
$b + $c as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Visualforce Page API Version",
	title_zh: "检测到 Visualforce API 版本低于 55",
	message: "Visualforce page API version is below 55.",
}
